{
  "id": "workflow-template-javascript-http-reader",
  "name": "http_reader",
  "rootNodeId": "template_root_javascript_http_reader",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "template_root_javascript_http_reader",
      "name": "http_reader",
      "kind": "Group",
      "children": [
        "http_reader"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "x": 40,
        "y": 40,
        "width": 500,
        "height": 240
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "http_reader",
      "name": "http_reader",
      "kind": "Processor",
      "parentId": "template_root_javascript_http_reader",
      "layout": {
        "x": 100,
        "y": 115,
        "width": 260,
        "height": 90
      },
      "technology": {
        "languageId": "javascript",
        "technologyId": "nodejs",
        "compilerId": "nodejs-compiler"
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "config",
          "name": "config",
          "direction": "Input",
          "dataType": "HttpRequestConfig"
        },
        {
          "id": "result",
          "name": "result",
          "direction": "Output",
          "dataType": "HttpResult"
        }
      ],
      "text": {
        "source": "const state = context.__httpReader ??= { busy: false };\nif (!state.busy && config.length > 0) {\n  const settings = config.shift();\n  if (!settings?.url) throw new Error(\"http_reader requires config.url\");\n  state.busy = true;\n  const query = new URLSearchParams(settings.params || {}).toString();\n  const method = String(settings.method || \"GET\").toUpperCase();\n  const url = query && method === \"GET\" ? `${settings.url}?${query}` : settings.url;\n  fetch(url, { method, headers: settings.headers || {}, body: query && method !== \"GET\" ? query : undefined }).then(async reply => { result.push({ status: reply.status, headers: Object.fromEntries(reply.headers), content: await reply.text() }); }).finally(() => { state.busy = false; });\n}",
        "specification": "Polls an HTTP endpoint from configuration and emits the received content into the network.\n\nPort contract: input port/link `config` supplies `HttpRequestConfig`; output port/link `result` emits `HttpResult` packets.\n\nConfiguration contains exactly the request controls `method`, `url`, `params`, and `headers`. `method` defaults to GET only when absent; `url` is required; `params` are encoded according to the method; `headers` are copied without allowing transport-owned headers to become inconsistent.\n\nEach polling cycle must be bounded and non-blocking with respect to network progress. Emit a result only after a complete response. Preserve status, response headers, and content in the effective `HttpResult` model, and route transport failures through the project's error policy rather than emitting partial content.",
        "aiInstructions": "Use the configured method, URL, params, and headers exactly. Respect timeouts and avoid overlapping polls unless explicitly configured."
      }
    }
  ]
}
